=== SURVEY ===
Mapped web `components/data-display` + `vehicles`: metric/status, lists/timelines, playback, people/vehicles,
and the 15 SI/unit formatting components. Reused tokens + P3-0001 UI (TSCard/TSBadge/TSIconBox/TSButton/
TSStatusDot) + TSChartPalette. SI formatters bind to the P1 `Units` facade.

=== REASONING ===
- Shared-coupling split: SI formatters (TSDistance/Speed/Temperature/Pressure/Energy/Power/Duration) call the
  KMP `Units` facade → Shared.xcframework, so they live in UnitFormatters.swift, EXCLUDED from the host
  swiftc -typecheck (like SharedFacade) and validated by P1's Units golden-vector test + the deferred build.
  The non-SI formatters (Currency/FormattedNumber/Percentage/Voltage/Current/DateTime/Range) need no facade →
  kept in TypedFormatters.swift and fully typechecked + unit-tested. All formatters render "—" for nil/non-finite.
- Reduce Motion: TSAnimatedNumber (.numericText), TSLiveIndicator pulse, etc. gate animations on
  accessibilityReduceMotion.
- Accessibility: badges/dots carry labels; metrics combine; live/progress expose accessibilityValue.
- Playback: keyboard shortcuts (space / arrows) on the transport controls (work with HW keyboard on iOS too).
- Real props: every component takes real state (values, bindings, callbacks) — no placeholder shells.

